{
    "name": "FullModelsLateral",
    "_comment_en": "BJT small-signal template for the lateral PNP - Full level (Analog Insydes LPNP branch of DoBJTSmallSignal, simp==0). Identical to the vertical FullModels EXCEPT the substrate capacitances: for the lateral device BOTH C_js and C_xs attach to the base, between the base port B and the substrate node S (the vertical model instead puts a single C_js at the collector, CS-0). Internal nodes BS/CS/ES are created by rx/rc/re; when a parasitic resolves to 0 the degeneracy cleanup shorts that port to its internal node and the level collapses (Full -> Simplified -> Basic) exactly as AI's simp rules prescribe. rc/re are read from the .out BJT MODEL PARAMETERS table; all symbol values are resolved in netlist/Model.py._bjt_ac_param_values. Requires a 4-terminal device (C B E S); the substrate port S is optional in AI and, when the netlist device has only 3 terminals, the C_js/C_xs branch to S is left dangling.",
